    "4.6.1 Use Case Diagram": 29,
    "1. SOC Analyst (Tier-1 / Tier-2): Logs into the platform with Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA), monitors the real-time alert queue, reviews AI-generated investigation summaries, runs natural-language search queries, and submits feedback to help train the ML models.": 30,
    "2. Detection Engineer: Creates and tests new detection rules (Sigma/YARA), manages threat intelligence feeds, and configures noise-filtering thresholds.": 30,
    "3. SOC Lead / Incident Commander: Reviews overall security metrics and approves high-impact containment actions (such as isolating critical servers).": 30,
    "4. Compliance Auditor / CISO: Inspects the tamper-evident audit ledger and exports signed compliance PDF reports for regulatory audits.": 30,
    "5. Autonomous AI Engine (System Actor): Automatically receives logs, removes duplicates, runs multi-agent AI investigations, and safely executes low-risk response actions in the background.": 30,
    "4.6.2 Activity Diagram": 30,
    "4.6.3 Sequence Diagram": 31,
    "1. The analyst opens the web console to view an incoming alert.": 32,
    "2. The web console requests alert details from the Central Management Backend.": 32,
    "3. The backend starts the Multi-Agent AI investigation.": 32,
    "4. The AI agents query the Neo4j graph database to see which other devices are connected to the infected computer.": 32,
    "5. The AI agents generate an investigation report and suggest a containment plan.": 32,
    "6. The report is pushed live to the analyst's screen.": 32,
    "7. The analyst reviews the summary and clicks 'Approve Containment.'": 32,
