    "5.5 Cryptographic Security and Data Protection": 39,
    "1. Network Transport Encryption: All network traffic between web browsers, API services, and microservices is encrypted using TLS 1.3 (HTTPS and secure WebSockets).": 39,
    "2. Secure Credential Vault: Third-party API keys (such as firewall passwords and cloud access tokens) are encrypted before being saved in the database using strong AES-128-CBC encryption with HMAC authentication.": 39,
    "3. Multi-Tenant Data Isolation: In shared environments, each organization's data is strictly separated using PostgreSQL Row-Level Security (RLS), ensuring that one organization can never see another organization's security alerts.": 39,
