    "7.4 System Verification and Automated Test Cases": 53,
    "7.5 Case Study: Step-by-Step Lateral Movement Investigation": 53,
    "1. Ingestion: The log ingestion worker received the login logs and automatically tagged the attack techniques.": 53,
    "2. Deduplication & Scoring: The system grouped 14 related login attempts into a single case ticket and calculated a high anomaly score of 89.4.": 53,
    "3. Multi-Agent Investigation: The AI agents traced the path in the Neo4j graph, showing that the compromised workstation had made an unauthorized connection to the database server. The agents searched historical logs, discovered a hidden PowerShell command, and drafted an incident summary.": 54,
    "4. Safe Containment: Because the database server was marked as high-priority, the system paused automatic isolation and sent an approval prompt to the security lead. Once approved, the infected workstation was disconnected from the network in 320 milliseconds.": 54,
